FFmpeg — LGPL v2.1 or later
--------------------------
This package configures FFmpeg (pinned to release n9.0.2) with decoders,
demuxers, parsers, bitstream filters, and minimal network/HTTPS support, and
WITHOUT --enable-gpl, so the result is LGPL, not GPL. The static libraries
(libavcodec, libavformat, libavutil, libswresample) and any binary that
statically links them are subject to the LGPL, including the section 6
relinking obligation: a distributor of such a binary must enable recipients to
relink it against a modified FFmpeg. The means to do so are provided by this
repository: the exact FFmpeg version and the full configure flag set are in
build.zig, and the object archives are the release tarballs. The full LGPL
v2.1 text is bundled with the release tarball as COPYING.LGPLv2.1. FFmpeg
licensing: https://www.ffmpeg.org/legal.html

TLS backends (HTTPS)
--------------------
HTTPS uses a platform-native or system TLS stack; none of these are GPL:
  - Windows: Schannel (OS component; link secur32, crypt32, ws2_32)
  - Linux: OpenSSL via pkg-config / libssl (Apache-2.0 for OpenSSL 3.x;
    consumer links ssl and crypto)
  - macOS: Secure Transport (OS frameworks Security + CoreFoundation)
OpenSSL is not bundled in the release archives; Linux consumers use the
system/OpenSSL they link against.

dav1d — BSD 2-Clause
--------------------
AV1 decoding uses libdav1d (VideoLAN), pinned to 1.5.4, statically linked.
FFmpeg's built-in av1 decoder is hardware-only; libdav1d provides software AV1.
License (BSD 2-Clause): bundled with the release tarball as COPYING.dav1d;
upstream at https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d/-/blob/master/COPYING

Vulkan-Headers — Apache License 2.0 / MIT
-----------------------------------------
The release tarball also contains the Khronos Vulkan headers (KhronosGroup/
Vulkan-Headers, pinned to v1.4.321) under include/vulkan and include/vk_video.
FFmpeg's Vulkan video decode support is built against them, and
libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.h includes <vulkan/vulkan.h>, so consumers need the
same headers to use that API. They are dual-licensed Apache-2.0 OR MIT; the full
texts are in the upstream repository under LICENSES/ at
https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Headers

